# OneWoW Player Wiki

`wiki/` is the **player** documentation surface. It syncs one-way to the GitHub
Wiki tab via `.github/workflows/publish-wiki.yml` (`Andrew-Chen-Wang/github-wiki-action`).
Never instruct editing pages in the GitHub Wiki UI — the next push from `main`
overwrites them.

Engineering Docs (`OneWoW/Docs/`, `ADDON/Docs/`) and code remain the source of
truth. When wiki and Docs disagree, fix the wiki.

## Page mechanics

- **No leading `#` H1** — GitHub Wiki already titles the page from the filename
  (`Bags-Search-Syntax.md` → “Bags Search Syntax”).
- **Flat layout** — all pages in `wiki/` root. Shared chrome only:
  `_Sidebar.md`, `_Footer.md`.
- **Filenames** — use dashes for multi-word titles; keep basenames unique.
- **LF only** — repo-wide; never CRLF.
- **Homepage** — `Home.md` (not `README.md`).

## Related → Sources

Every content page ends with:

```markdown
## Related

* …wiki and in-game pointers…

### Sources

* [path](https://github.com/kellewic/OneWoW_Suite/blob/main/path) — …
```

**Sources must use explicit `blob/main/` URLs.** Relative `../README.md` links are
**not** rewritten correctly for the wiki tab (they become
`github.com/…/OneWoW_Suite/README.md` without `/blob/main/`). Absolute `https://`
links pass through the Action’s preprocess unchanged.

## Content rules

- **Rewrite, don’t paste Docs.** Strip API surfaces, file maps, agent/implementer
  notes, and SV schema. Player example: wiki `Bags-Search-Syntax` vs
  `OneWoW_Bags/Docs/SEARCH_SYNTAX.md`.
- **One feature ≈ one overview page**; long how-tos (search syntax) get their own page.
- **Developers** page stays thin — commentary + links into repo Docs, not a second Docs tree.
- **Do not** document AccountSync or similar non-player package tools on the wiki
  unless product policy explicitly changes.
- Keywords in search docs stay **English-only**; say so when relevant.

## Catalog parity (new feature module)

When adding a public feature load unit, update together:

1. Root `README.md` (catalog table + mermaid if present)
2. `ADDON/README.md` (player overview)
3. `wiki/<Feature>.md` + `_Sidebar.md` (and Home feature table if listed)
4. `OneWoW/Docs/README.md` feature-addons index when contributor Docs exist

## Publish

- Workflow: path-filtered push to `main` on `wiki/**` (+ the workflow file).
- `contents: write`; `disable-empty-commits: true`; action `@v5`.
- Wiki backend must already exist (one-time dummy page in GitHub UI — already done
  for this repo).
